data.value:
Close whatever is holding the trusted phones' file, then choose Forget all again, or delete it yourself:

{0}

The trusted phones could not be forgotten: their file could not be removed or emptied. No phone can connect while Edgepad stays running, but those phones will be trusted again the next time Edgepad starts.

Choose Forget all again, or delete pin-verified.txt yourself from:

{0}

The phones that entered the PIN could not be forgotten: their list could not be removed. While Edgepad stays running every phone is asked for the PIN on every connection, but those phones will skip it at level 2 again the next time Edgepad starts.

Choose Forget all again, or delete paired-links.txt yourself from:

{0}

The Wi-Fi and USB pairings could not be forgotten: their file could not be removed or emptied. Paired phones cannot reconnect over Wi-Fi or USB while Edgepad stays running, but they will be able to again the next time it starts.

Close whatever is holding the file, then choose Reset again, or delete it yourself:

{0}

Nothing was reset: the trusted phones could not be forgotten, so the PIN and the level were left as they were. No phone can connect while Edgepad stays running, but those phones will be trusted again, behind the same PIN, the next time it starts.

Close whatever is holding the file, then choose Reset again, or delete security.txt and pin-verified.txt yourself from:

{0}

The trusted phones were forgotten, but the PIN could not be reset: a settings file could not be removed, so the old PIN and level may still apply. Each phone has to be trusted here again.
